# Generated by `npm run harvest`. Prettier and the generator would rewrite each
# other on every run, leaving the tree permanently dirty.
#
# Listed by name rather than globbed: inventory/ also holds HAND-AUTHORED files
# — README.md and task-vocabulary.yaml — which prettier SHOULD format, and a
# `*.yaml` glob silently excluded the vocabulary the day it was added.
inventory/charter-documents.yaml
inventory/charter-services.yaml
inventory/office-pages.yaml
inventory/site-pages.yaml
inventory/source-notes.md

# Generated by `npm run charter:pages` and `npm run charter:extract`, and the
# reason is the same as the harvest above with one extra edge.
#
# 🔴 Prettier ALIGNS markdown tables — it pads every cell in a column to the
# widest one. A charter's client-steps table has one cell running to a paragraph
# and five hundred that do not, so every row was padded to 1,780 characters and
# the building-permit page reached **1.17 MB**, almost all of it spaces.
#
# Scoped to the generated trees. `content/` also holds hand-authored pages — the
# emergency layer, the home copy, the history — and those SHOULD be formatted.
content/services/
content/government/legislative/
content/charter/
inventory/charter-transcripts/
inventory/charter-completeness.json
inventory/charter-extraction-report.yaml
